cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Please also cite the source of the bundled dictionary (references)."
title: "torturedcheck: tortured-phrase detection for academic documents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Feldman
    given-names: Gilad
    affiliation: University of Innsbruck
version: "0.1.2"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/giladfeldman/torturedcheck"
abstract: >-
  A TypeScript library that scans academic text for tortured phrases, the nonsensical
  synonym substitutions left by paraphrasing tools, using a bundled snapshot of the
  Problematic Paper Screener dictionary, and rates the document with a density-aware
  risk level.
keywords:
  - tortured phrases
  - paper mills
  - research integrity
  - meta-science
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Tortured phrases: A dubious writing style emerging in science. Evidence of critical issues affecting established journals"
    authors:
      - family-names: Cabanac
        given-names: Guillaume
      - family-names: Labbé
        given-names: Cyril
      - family-names: Magazinov
        given-names: Alexander
    year: 2021
    doi: "10.48550/arXiv.2107.06751"
